#NEXUS

[ averianov2018b_fig6: Titanosaur tree, read by eye; every child leaves its node on a diagonal, so a node is the point where the diagonals meet. Lithostrotia, Saltasauridae and Lognkosauria (spelled as printed), joined to nodes by leader lines, are kept as internal labels; the support digits are not. Polytomies: the root (six tips and the rest), the five-tip node beside the Isisaurus-Saltasauridae clade, Pitekunsaurus-Volgatitan-the rest, Muyelensaurus-Rinconsaurus-Lognkosauria, and Notocolossus-Patagotitan-Puertasaurus. 35 tips, 5 polytomies (7, 6, 3, 3, 3 children); 3 printed clade names kept as internal node labels. Sample 6 case (census 2 extended to draw 120, seed 20261231). Topology transcribed from the figure image and checked node by node; topology only. ]

